> Trace an executed native operation

The block graph is traced from the actual operation below. Named stages mark its semantic endpoints; the complete program supplies the source geometry and parameter census.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/deep_boltzmann_network.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");n::ParameterStore p(23003);m::DeepBoltzmannParameters(p);n::Module model([&](const n::Tensor& x){auto y=m::DbmUnnormalized(p,x);n::model_stage("Exact16-state posterior",x,y.hidden1_posterior);return n::model_stage("Unnormalized log mass",y.hidden1_posterior,y.log_weight);},"deep boltzmann: native operation");n::ModelPlotOptions o;o.detail=n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;o.sizing.minimum_extent=2;o.sizing.max_planes=2;model.plot(n::zeros({1,8}),o).save_svg("build/deep_boltzmann_network.svg");}
